{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772810-dealing-with-spirits","id":772810,"title":"Dealing with spirits.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-23T21:59:24-08:00","id":772810,"title":"Dealing with spirits.","content":"A few questions, because I couldn't find answers in the book. I'm running a game and a theurge character will join at some point, and I'm not sure what to do.<br /> <br /> How does a player contact a spirit in the material world? Can they merely use spirit speech and talk into the fire, asking it to spread favourably, or encourage a machine spirit to break down. Or do players have to summon a spirit, get it to materialise, and then have it effect whatever it is. There are spirit related gifts that are more specific about what they can and can't do. are those what are required to go full wolf-mage? What is?<br /> <br /> Do black spiral dancers deal with non-bane spirits.? They don't seem to have a way to soak silver like gaian garou do. (not that I'm entirely sure when it comes to armour gifts. Luna's blessing definitely does, troll's hide doesn't. Steel fur is a maybe, the wyrm one might be a maybe... ) No, being a gaian garou, learning gifts and then walking the spiral doesn't count for this.<br /> <br /> Revised states that all charms have correlative gifts. How true is this? Can a garou be summoning fires, firing atomic blasts, calcifying enemies and so on?<br /> <br /> If the gift that changes the properties of a spirit is used on a bane to change the fact that it's a bane, what happens to the rest of the nature of the spirit? Do we get a good guy-scrag murder spirit or benevolent balefire.<br /> Then again; I'm not sure why a spirit of war isn't considered a bane. (or does spirit of war not actually specifically mean there is a spirit 'of war' but rather simply a warlike spirit of something else)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-23T23:53:31-08:00","id":772852,"title":"","content":"First yes there are gifts that let you summon fire create element at the low end and balefire at the high end. War spirits and pain and death are all aspects of a bigger thing. You may have a pain spirit of a paper cut, and another associated with withdrawal. Spirits are flexible. Unless the fire has an awakened aspect/materialized spirit speaking to it in the real world probably won't work. Stepping sideways and dealing with spirits in the Umbra is better. Changing a spirit creates a new spirit. BSD retain Breed immunity to silver and most of the Auspice gifts remain the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T00:53:16-08:00","id":772865,"title":"","content":"Building off what Incbill said, a spirit that is redeemed by the Garou is likely going to need a new patron and it would be best to find it a brood that would be familiar to it. If a pack manages to save a ravening spirit of gluttony from the Wyrm, that being might go to Wendigo, if the great cannibal spirit would deign to accept it. A spirit freed from its service to Foebok may find a place among the brood of Grandfather Thunder, if it is found worthy... you get the idea.<br /> <br /> And as for War spirits not being of the Wyrm, there are a lot of reasons why this is the case. Violence and killing are not evil to the Garou (you will note the lack of anything resembling a VtM humanity morality meter). I would posit that the idea of 'just war' is a central theme to WtA, as war is exactly what the Garou were created to do: wage war on the Wyrm and its minions. War is merely orchestrated violence, after all, and violence is not essentially 'of the Wyrm.' A lot of Wyrmish atrocities might be committed in war, but that does not mean the entire concept is tainted and that the beings associated with warfare are inherently evil. There are spirits that directly represent war (Dogs of War in Axis Mundi are an example, and the totem Ares/Clashing Boom-Boom is another). There are spirits that are indirectly tied to war also, such as weapon spirits like Hunter-Killers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-24-2015, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T01:03:38-08:00","id":772866,"title":"","content":"There is &quot;War&quot; as the ideal. The grand battle. The glorious heroes. Weapons of Legend. Honor and Glory.<br /> There is &quot;War&quot; as opportunity, innovation, technology, strength.<br /> There is &quot;War&quot; as suffering, civilian casualties, death in the trenches, gangrene, amputations and PTSP<br /> <br /> There is &quot;Pain&quot; as the ideal. The impulse that teaches you not to do what you should not be doing.<br /> There is &quot;Pain&quot; as heartbreak. Loss. Depression<br /> There is &quot;Pain&quot; Torture. The Lingering Death. Spousal Abuse.<br /> <br /> They are different concepts and as such are represented by different spirits. Spirits are ideals and concepts given shape, not well weighed rational explanations of terms.<br /> <br /> You have to summon a spirit to talk with it, using an appropriate rite. The fire and the electrical wiring do not have functional spirits, so you're stuck with spirits that are actually available. Nota bene, the fire and the electrical wiring can be made into spirits, but it requires a rite, spiritual intervention or love and care. For instance, the hot rod that was lovingly built over a decade, painted and rebuilt only to be driven with the gentlest hand, caressed and called Betty could have a spirit of its own. Summoning is the key in all Spirit relationships, and it's what makes a good shaman. Combo it with good social skills and a knack for motivating them to do what you want them to, and you will be a legend.<br /> <br /> Materialisation is not necessary at all times, since some summoned spirits have the ability to commune accross the gauntlet, but even if they cannot, the Garou can easily pop over to the other side.<br /> <br /> Black Spiral Dancers deal with what ever spirits they want. Whether or not those spirits want their attention or care to help is another matter altogether. They can soak non-lethal silver in their breed forms, unless they are metis. Outside that, they need gifts. Gifts soak siliver only if they specifically say they soak silver. BSD's have access to most gifts that the Garou have, so some of them will have gifts allowing them to soak silver.<br /> <br /> Gifts are specialised expressions of Charms native to the Garou. Yes, in theory every Charm can be mapped to a Gift and vice versa. They are not in practice because you want a simple system for spirits to make them simpler to use on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T10:15:38-08:00","id":773230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772810-dealing-with-spirits#post772810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does a player contact a spirit in the material world?</div> </div> </div> </div>You either need to encounter the spirit (likely in the Umbra unless it has manifested in the Realm), or perform the Rite of Summoning. Once the spirit is in front of you, you can then interact with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772810-dealing-with-spirits#post772810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can they merely use spirit speech and talk into the fire, asking it to spread favourably, or encourage a machine spirit to break down.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Even if there is a spirit active in the Penumbra, that is not enough. The Gauntlet is a barrier and unless you use a Gift or other power to observe/interact with the other side, you can't.<br /> <br /> Most objects in the Realm do not have an awakened spirit with which you can interact with anyway. Usually you would first need to perform the Rite of Spirit Awakening to rouse it from slumber, and then you could interact with it.<br /> <br /> Also bear in mind that most spirits are Gafflings and have the intelligence of an animal. Unlike animals, they can &quot;speak&quot; but they are not capable of complex thought an any conversation will be very basic. You can have real intelligent conversations with Jagglings which have individual personalities, but those won't be in any specific object. They are more &quot;general&quot; spirits of that nature created by the Incarnas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772810-dealing-with-spirits#post772810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are spirit related gifts that are more specific about what they can and can't do. are those what are required to go full wolf-mage? What is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Theurge Gifts and Mystic Rites are what you need.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772810-dealing-with-spirits#post772810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do black spiral dancers deal with non-bane spirits.?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can, but Gaian spirits will be hostile to them and not want to interact with them unless under force. However, Corrupted Gaian spirits also serve the Wyrm, and those technically are not Banes. Bat was a canonically example of that. I'd use a handful of &quot;normal&quot; spirits commonly associated with evil or witchcraft to reflect those - toads, black cats, etc. - although not all spirits of that kind would be corrupt. There are also spirits of the old Balance Wyrm that remain loyal to Gaia; I imagine interaction with them by the BSD to be similar to contacting an ex. The spirits likely won't want to talk with you, but there would be various reasons why they would. Some spirits that are neither Banes nor Gaian (like many Enigmatic spirits or Chimerlings) might not care that the BSD's serve the Wyrm and would neither be particularly friendly or hostile.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772810-dealing-with-spirits#post772810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revised states that all charms have correlative gifts. How true is this? Can a garou be summoning fires, firing atomic blasts, calcifying enemies and so on?</div> </div> </div> </div>Charms aren't Gifts although many do have Gifts that are very similar, and I think that is what Revised meant. You just need to find (or possibly invent) the Gift that is similar. There are no charts listing all the Gifts a spirit can teach. This is really up to the ST as to what Gifts are appropriate for each spirit to teach.<br /> <br /> If a player wants to use the actual Charm, what is most appropriate is for the character to summon the spirit who has it and pay the appropriate chiminage for the spirit to use it, or create an appropriate Fetish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772810-dealing-with-spirits#post772810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the gift that changes the properties of a spirit is used on a bane to change the fact that it's a bane, what happens to the rest of the nature of the spirit? Do we get a good guy-scrag murder spirit or benevolent balefire.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it comes to spirits, I believe form equals function. Balefires and Scrags are inherently tainted because of their nature. You'd have to change them into a non-tainted equivalent. Balefire might be turned into a normal Fire spirit or perhaps an Electrical spirit (if the balefire is a result of atomic power used in a nuclear power plant). There are different kind of Scrags, but you'd need to do something similar. It is not just changing traits, but turning it into something appropriate which will take some creativity and logic.<br /> <br /> If we want to do the inverse of &quot;corrupting a Gaian spirit&quot;, I guess it is possible to have a good guy-scrag murder spirit or benevolent balefire, but I don't think such changes could work long. Such a spirit will either revert back given where it naturally resides or be destroyed by others like it. It would be more like the old Charm Person in D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/772810-dealing-with-spirits#post772810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again; I'm not sure why a spirit of war isn't considered a bane. (or does spirit of war not actually specifically mean there is a spirit 'of war' but rather simply a warlike spirit of something else)</div> </div> </div> </div>War in and of itself does not have any particular value. People fear death, but death is a natural part of life. Violence exists in the normal course of a predator hunting its prey. Both the aggressor unjustly attacking his neighbor, and those simply defending their homes are equal participants.<br /> <br /> War is a universal phenomenon among Mankind and even other animals such as chimpanzees, wolves, lions, and ants. As such, it may even part of the &quot;Gaian order&quot;.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf cosmology, a Spirit of War is likely an Epiph and thus a platonic ideal divorced from the usual Gaian spirits and their role in the ecosystem.<br /> <br /> Of course, war leads to many evil things, and it is likely a host of Banes eagerly follow or are associated with a spirit of War in the same way scavengers follow the big prey animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}